WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.100
Narrator: In a car park, drivers can't hear you, so your hands and arms communicate instructions.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.600
Narrator: Use only the approved signals.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:16.300
Narrator: Never make up your own signals, because drivers and other marshals must know exactly what you mean.

4
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:22.600
Narrator: Stop: one arm extended straight forwards, with an open palm towards the driver.

5
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.300
Narrator: Come forward: both hands beckoning motion towards you.

6
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:34.500
Narrator: Slow down: arm fully extended to side, palm down, arm moving up and down.

7
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:42.900
Narrator: Turn: point direction of travel with appropriate side arm extended, use other hand to beckon in that direction.

8
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:51.500
Narrator: Stop here: hands apart, closing to show the distance left, fully cross arms to indicate the stop.

9
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.300
Narrator: Emergency stop: both arms fully extended, palms to the driver.

10
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:04.800
Narrator: Keep every signal big, slow and clear, make eye contact, and give one signal at a time.
